    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #263\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch pushed: `bb/relay-195-mail-live-sync-01-06-host-long-lived-l-thr_9dry56d5u5`\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #195's mailsync composition root in `backend/packages/data/src/mail/mailLiveSyncRoot.ts`:\n\n- **`createMailLiveSyncRoot(pool, mailboxesDatabaseId, lifecycleFactory, options)`** discovers active (non-soft-deleted) Mailbox accounts and hosts exactly one lifecycle per account, stopping it on deactivation (soft-delete) and restarting it if the account's `sync_mode` changes.\n- Restart-safety: only ever reads/seeds persisted `mail_account_sync_state` (via the existing `ensureMailAccountSyncState`), never resets it — a fresh process rediscovers the same active accounts without duplicating watchers.\n- Failure isolation: per-account try/catch around discovery, start, and stop, surfaced via an optional `onLifecycleError` callback, so one account's failure never blocks others.\n- `createNoopMailLiveSyncLifecycleFactory` is the default lifecycle (no real transport yet — provider transports are out of scope for this issue, deferred to #196+); it enqueues an immediate pass through the existing idempotent, jobKey-deduplicated `mailAccountSync` job, and the interface docs make explicit that any future live signal must go through that same path rather than a parallel ingestion route.\n- Exported from `index.ts` alongside the existing `createCoreTaskList`/`CORE_CRONTAB`.\n- Added `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/mailLiveSyncRoot.test.ts` covering: one lifecycle per active account, stop-on-deactivation with isolation, restart restoring persisted state without duplicate watchers, per-account failure isolation, and lifecycle restart on sync-mode change.\n\nVerified: full backend suite passes (19 test files, 253 tests, exit code 0). `tsc` shows no new errors from this change; one pre-existing, unrelated `tsc` error in `inboxPipeline.test.ts` already exists identically on `origin/develop`.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
